{
  "subject": "Kaveri Cements: Rs 47.50 cr of MSMED interest in your own filings",
  "opening": "Your FY2025 accounts disclose Rs 310.00 cr owed to micro and small suppliers past the appointed day, and Rs 47.50 cr of interest accrued on it. That is 1.131% of revenue, and it accrues whether or not a supplier ever raises it. Worth asking who inside the business watches the 45 day clock, and which system tells them when it breaks."
}

{
  "subject": "Kaveri Cements: Rs 126.00 cr leaking through accounts payable"            ,
  "opening": "Across FY2025 your filings point to roughly Rs 126.00 cr of avoidable cost in accounts payable, about 3.2% of revenue, and peers in cement run materially tighter on supplier payment. Most of it traces back to manual invoice matching, which is exactly the kind of thing that disappears once the process is automated end to end."
}
